/-!
# The vocabulary of Ergodic Generative Flows: generative flows, EGFs, universal families, summable `L²`-mixing

**`def:summably_mixing`** — `main.tex:262`

`def:egf` — `main.tex:216` (not marked: the "group" of the sentence and the words of its "that is"
clause differ, a question for the author; see SCOPE)

`def:universal_family` — `main.tex:249` (not marked: "distributions" read as probability measures;
see SCOPE)

The generative-flow vocabulary of the preliminaries (`main.tex:158`, `:161`, `:183`, `:196`, `:316`)
is defined here too, since every later EGF module reads it.

> A generative flow on $\Statespace$ is the data of a star forward policy, i.e. a Markov kernel
> $\ForwardPolicyStar:\Statespace\rightarrow \Statespace$, and a star outflow, i.e. a finite
> non-negative measure $\Foutstar$ on $\Statespace$. (`main.tex:161`)

> A Markov kernel $\pi$ on $(\Statespace,\lambda)$ is summably $L^2$-mixing if $\pi$ admits an
> invariant measure $\widehat \lambda$ equivalent to $\lambda$ and such that the $L^2$-mixing
> coefficients given by,
> $\gamma_n := \sup_{\varphi \in H} \int_{s\in \Statespace} \left(\varphi\pi^n(s)\right)^2
> d\widehat \lambda(s)$,
> with $H = \{\varphi \in L^2(\lambda)~|~\|\varphi\|_2 = 1 \text{ and }
> \int_{s\in \Statespace} \varphi(s)=0\}$ are summable: $\sum_{n\geq 0} \gamma_n < +\infty$.
> (`main.tex:262–269`)

> This property is in particular satisfied if the policy $\pi$ induces a Koopman operator
> $\phi \mapsto \frac{d (\phi\lambda)\pi}{d\lambda}$ on $L^2(\Statespace)$, which has a so-called
> spectral gap. Informally the spectrum of the Koopman operator is bounded away from 1 on the
> subspace $\{\phi~|~\int \phi d\lambda =0\}$. (`main.tex:273`)

> Let $\Statespace$ be Riemannian manifold endowed with its volume measure $\lambda$ and let
> $(\Phi_{i})_{i=1}^p$ be a family of diffeomorphisms $\Statespace\rightarrow \Statespace$. An EGF
> is a generative flow, where
> $\ForwardPolicyStar(s) = \sum_{i=1}^p\forwardalpha^i(s) \delta_{\Phi_i(s)}$
> for some policy $\forwardalpha:\Statespace \rightarrow [0,1]^p$, and such that the group of
> diffeomorphisms generated by the $\Phi_i$ is topologically ergodic. That is for all
> $x,y \in \Statespace$ and any neighborhood $\mathcal U$ of $y$, there exists a sequence
> $i_1,\cdots, i_t$ such that $x\Phi_{i_1}\Phi_{i_2}\cdots \Phi_{i_t} \in \mathcal U$.
> (`main.tex:216–222`)

> On a state space $(\Statespace,\lambda)$, a family of generative flow family is universal if for
> any two distributions $\mu,\nu\ll \lambda$ with bounded density there is a flow
> $(\foutstar,\ForwardPolicyStar)$ in the family that is flow matching for $\Finit=\nu$ and
> $\Fterm=\mu$. (`main.tex:249–252`)

## What is defined and proved

| | |
|---|---|
| `GenerativeFlow` | a Markov kernel (star forward policy) and a finite measure (star outflow), `main.tex:161` |
| `inflow`, `IsFlowMatching` | `F_in = F_out π` (`main.tex:196`); `F_init + F_out π = F_term + F_out` (`main.tex:183`) |
| `initialError`, `terminalError` | `δF_init`, `δF_term` (`main.tex:316`); `initialError_eq_negPart`, `terminalError_eq_posPart`: the Jordan parts of `F_init + F_in − F_term − F_out` |
| `pushIter`, `transfer` | `μπⁿ`, and `φπⁿ := d((φλ)πⁿ)/dλ`, the Koopman operator of `main.tex:273` |
| `unitMeanZero`, `mixingCoeff`, **`IsSummablyL2Mixing`** | `H`, `γₙ`, `def:summably_mixing` |
| `IsEGFPolicy`, `egfKernel`, `isEGFPolicy_egfKernel`, `IsEGFPolicy.isMarkovKernel` | `π(s) = ∑ᵢ αⁱ(s) δ_{Φᵢ(s)}`; it exists and is Markov |
| `IsTopologicallyErgodic`, `IsEGF` | the "that is" clause of `def:egf`, and `def:egf` |
| `isTopologicallyErgodic_iff_pos` | with `p ≥ 1` maps, allowing the empty word (`t = 0`) changes nothing |
| `IsTopologicallyErgodicGroup`, `IsTopologicallyErgodic.group`, `shiftZ_group_not_forward` | the group reading; the clause implies it, and not conversely (translation on `ℤ`) |
| `IsUniversalFamily`, `IsUniversalFamilyUnnormalized`, `not_isUniversalFamilyUnnormalized` | `def:universal_family`, its other reading, and that reading is never satisfied |

## Hypothesis checklist

| paper | here |
|---|---|
| `π` Markov, `λ̂` invariant, `λ̂ ~ λ` (`def:summably_mixing`) | ✓ `λ̂.bind π = λ̂`, `λ̂ ≪ λ`, `λ ≪ λ̂`; `λ̂` any measure, as printed (not assumed finite) |
| `φπⁿ` | ✓ `d((φλ)πⁿ)/dλ` (`main.tex:273`), through `φ⁺`, `φ⁻` |
| `H`: `φ ∈ L²(λ)`, `‖φ‖₂ = 1`, `∫ φ = 0` | ✓ `MemLp φ 2 λ`, `eLpNorm φ 2 λ = 1`, `∫ φ ∂λ = 0` (the measure of `main.tex:273`) |
| `∑ γₙ < +∞` | ✓ `∑' n, γₙ ≠ ∞`, `γₙ ∈ [0, ∞]` |
| `𝒮` a Riemannian manifold with its volume (`def:egf`) | ⚠ weakened: a topological space with a σ-algebra; `IsEGF` does not read `λ` |
| `Φᵢ` diffeomorphisms | ⚠ weakened: measurable homeomorphisms `𝒮 ≃ₜ 𝒮` |
| `α : 𝒮 → [0,1]^p` | ✓ plus `∑ᵢ αⁱ = 1`, which "an EGF is a generative flow" (a Markov kernel) forces; ⚠ measurability of `α` is a mild added condition (the paper's `α` is a softmax head, `main.tex:288`, `:386`; on a standard Borel space a measurable `α` giving the same `π` exists) |
| topological ergodicity | ? the "that is" clause verbatim (forward words, `t ≥ 0`); the group reading is `IsTopologicallyErgodicGroup` |
| "two distributions `μ, ν ≪ λ` with bounded density" | ? probability measures, `dμ/dλ ≤ C` `λ`-a.e. |

## SCOPE (disclosed)

**`def:summably_mixing` is marked.** `φπⁿ` is not defined for a function at `main.tex:158`; the
next paragraph (`main.tex:273`) names the operator, `φ ↦ d((φλ)π)/dλ`, and the mean-zero subspace,
`∫ φ dλ = 0`; the proof of `theo:universality_true` uses both (`main.tex:788–789`: `εₜ(𝒮) = 0`, and
`dεₜ/dλ`). `transfer` takes the density of the absolutely continuous part of `(φλ)πⁿ`; under the
definition's own invariance `λ̂π = λ̂ ~ λ` that measure is `≪ λ`, and iterating the one-step operator
gives the same density. The definition writes `∫ φ(s)` with no measure (finding). The paper only ever uses the definition
with `λ̂ = λ`, where this transfer, the transfer of `L²(λ̂)` and the Markov operator on functions give
the same `γₙ`; for `λ̂ ≠ λ` they differ, and the REPORT asks the author to confirm the reading taken
(both marks rest on it).

**`def:egf` is not marked.** The sentence names the *group* generated by the `Φᵢ`; its "that is"
clause uses words in the `Φᵢ` only. `IsEGF` takes the clause; the two differ on non-compact spaces
(`shiftZ_group_not_forward`: the translation of `ℤ`), so which is meant is the author's call. The
generalization from a Riemannian manifold to a topological measurable space and from
diffeomorphisms to homeomorphisms is Lean ≥ paper (every diffeomorphism is a homeomorphism,
`Diffeomorph.toHomeomorph`, and the Borel σ-algebra makes it measurable).

**`def:universal_family` is not marked.** "Distributions" is read as *probability* measures. As
unnormalized measures the definition is never satisfied on a finite non-zero `λ`
(`not_isUniversalFamilyUnnormalized`), so that reading is excluded; equal-mass finite measures
would be a third reading, different for a family not closed under scaling the outflow.

Provenance: mathlib `fabf563a` (tag `v4.31.0`), pinned via `lakefile.toml`.
-/

namespace EGF

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter
open scoped ENNReal NNReal Topology

variable {S : Type*} [MeasurableSpace S]

/-! ## Generative flows (`main.tex:158–172`, `:316`) -/

/-- **A generative flow** (`main.tex:161`): a star forward policy, a Markov kernel `π : 𝒮 → 𝒮`,
and a star outflow, a finite non-negative measure `F_out` on `𝒮`. -/
structure GenerativeFlow (S : Type*) [MeasurableSpace S] where
  /-- The star forward policy `π`. -/
  policy : Kernel S S
  /-- The star outflow `F_out`. -/
  outflow : Measure S
  isMarkovKernel_policy : IsMarkovKernel policy
  isFiniteMeasure_outflow : IsFiniteMeasure outflow

attribute [instance] GenerativeFlow.isMarkovKernel_policy GenerativeFlow.isFiniteMeasure_outflow

/-- **The star inflow** `F_in = F_out π` (`main.tex:196`), the image measure of `main.tex:158`:
`(μπ)(A) = ∫ π(x)(A) dμ(x)`. -/
noncomputable def inflow (π : Kernel S S) (Fout : Measure S) : Measure S :=
  Fout.bind π

/-- **The flow-matching constraint** (`main.tex:183`): `F_init + F_out π = F_term + F_out`. -/
def IsFlowMatching (π : Kernel S S) (Fout Finit Fterm : Measure S) : Prop :=
  Finit + inflow π Fout = Fterm + Fout

/-- **The initial error** `δF_init := (F_init + F_in − F_term − F_out)⁻` (`main.tex:316`). For finite
measures Mathlib's truncated difference `A - B` is the positive part of the signed measure `A − B`,
so the negative part of `A − B` is `B - A`. -/
noncomputable def initialError (π : Kernel S S) (Fout Finit Fterm : Measure S) : Measure S :=
  (Fterm + Fout) - (Finit + inflow π Fout)

/-- **The terminal error** `δF_term := (F_init + F_in − F_term − F_out)⁺` (`main.tex:316`). -/
noncomputable def terminalError (π : Kernel S S) (Fout Finit Fterm : Measure S) : Measure S :=
  (Finit + inflow π Fout) - (Fterm + Fout)

/-- A Markov kernel preserves total mass: `(μπ)(𝒮) = μ(𝒮)`. -/
theorem bind_univ (π : Kernel S S) [IsMarkovKernel π] (μ : Measure S) :
    (μ.bind π) Set.univ = μ Set.univ := by
  rw [Measure.bind_apply MeasurableSet.univ (π.aemeasurable)]
  simp

instance isFiniteMeasure_bind (π : Kernel S S) [IsMarkovKernel π] (μ : Measure S)
    [IsFiniteMeasure μ] : IsFiniteMeasure (μ.bind π) :=
  ⟨by rw [bind_univ]; exact measure_lt_top _ _⟩

instance isFiniteMeasure_inflow (π : Kernel S S) [IsMarkovKernel π] (Fout : Measure S)
    [IsFiniteMeasure Fout] : IsFiniteMeasure (inflow π Fout) :=
  isFiniteMeasure_bind π Fout

/-- **`δF_term` is the positive part** of the signed measure `F_init + F_in − F_term − F_out`, in
Mathlib's Jordan decomposition (`main.tex:316`: "the positive and negative parts of a measure"). -/
theorem terminalError_eq_posPart (π : Kernel S S) [IsMarkovKernel π] (Fout Finit Fterm : Measure S)
    [IsFiniteMeasure Fout] [IsFiniteMeasure Finit] [IsFiniteMeasure Fterm] :
    terminalError π Fout Finit Fterm = ((Finit + inflow π Fout).toSignedMeasure
      - (Fterm + Fout).toSignedMeasure).toJordanDecomposition.posPart := by
  rw [Measure.toJordanDecomposition_toSignedMeasure_sub]; rfl

/-- **`δF_init` is the negative part** of the signed measure `F_init + F_in − F_term − F_out`. -/
theorem initialError_eq_negPart (π : Kernel S S) [IsMarkovKernel π] (Fout Finit Fterm : Measure S)
    [IsFiniteMeasure Fout] [IsFiniteMeasure Finit] [IsFiniteMeasure Fterm] :
    initialError π Fout Finit Fterm = ((Finit + inflow π Fout).toSignedMeasure
      - (Fterm + Fout).toSignedMeasure).toJordanDecomposition.negPart := by
  rw [Measure.toJordanDecomposition_toSignedMeasure_sub]; rfl

/-- A bundled generative flow is flow matching from `F_init` to `F_term`. -/
def GenerativeFlow.IsFlowMatching (F : GenerativeFlow S) (Finit Fterm : Measure S) : Prop :=
  EGF.IsFlowMatching F.policy F.outflow Finit Fterm

/-! ## Ergodic generative flows (`def:egf`, `main.tex:216–222`) -/

/-- **The forward policy of an EGF** (`main.tex:219`): `π(s) = ∑ᵢ αⁱ(s) δ_{Φᵢ(s)}`, with measurable
maps `Φᵢ` and a measurable policy `α` with values in the simplex. Template:
`GFNBounds.Core.EGF.IsEGFPolicy` (`lean/GFNBounds/Core/UniversalityBody.lean`), rewritten locally
(wave 0, `kb/0001`). -/
structure IsEGFPolicy (π : Kernel S S) {p : ℕ} (Φ : Fin p → S → S) (α : Fin p → S → ℝ) :
    Prop where
  measurable_map : ∀ i, Measurable (Φ i)
  measurable_weight : ∀ i, Measurable (α i)
  weight_nonneg : ∀ i s, 0 ≤ α i s
  weight_sum : ∀ s, ∑ i, α i s = 1
  apply_eq : ∀ s, π s = ∑ i, ENNReal.ofReal (α i s) • Measure.dirac (Φ i s)

/-- The kernel `s ↦ ∑ᵢ αⁱ(s) δ_{Φᵢ(s)}`, for measurable maps and weights (template:
`GFNBounds.Core.EGF.egfKernel`). -/
noncomputable def egfKernel {p : ℕ} (Φ : Fin p → S → S) (α : Fin p → S → ℝ)
    (hΦ : ∀ i, Measurable (Φ i)) (hα : ∀ i, Measurable (α i)) : Kernel S S where
  toFun s := ∑ i, ENNReal.ofReal (α i s) • Measure.dirac (Φ i s)
  measurable' := by
    refine Measure.measurable_of_measurable_coe _ fun A hA => ?_
    simp only [Measure.coe_finsetSum, Finset.sum_apply, Measure.smul_apply,
      Measure.dirac_apply' _ hA, smul_eq_mul]
    exact Finset.measurable_sum _ fun i _ =>
      (ENNReal.measurable_ofReal.comp (hα i)).mul
        ((measurable_const.indicator hA).comp (hΦ i))

/-- Every admissible choice of maps and policy is the forward policy of an EGF. -/
theorem isEGFPolicy_egfKernel {p : ℕ} (Φ : Fin p → S → S) (α : Fin p → S → ℝ)
    (hΦ : ∀ i, Measurable (Φ i)) (hα : ∀ i, Measurable (α i)) (hnn : ∀ i s, 0 ≤ α i s)
    (hsum : ∀ s, ∑ i, α i s = 1) : IsEGFPolicy (egfKernel Φ α hΦ hα) Φ α where
  measurable_map := hΦ
  measurable_weight := hα
  weight_nonneg := hnn
  weight_sum := hsum
  apply_eq _ := rfl

/-- The forward policy of an EGF is a Markov kernel: the weights sum to `1`. -/
theorem IsEGFPolicy.isMarkovKernel {π : Kernel S S} {p : ℕ} {Φ : Fin p → S → S}
    {α : Fin p → S → ℝ} (h : IsEGFPolicy π Φ α) : IsMarkovKernel π := by
  refine ⟨fun s => ⟨?_⟩⟩
  rw [h.apply_eq s, Measure.finsetSum_apply]
  simp only [Measure.smul_apply, measure_univ, smul_eq_mul, mul_one]
  rw [← ENNReal.ofReal_sum_of_nonneg (fun i _ => h.weight_nonneg i s), h.weight_sum s,
    ENNReal.ofReal_one]

/-- **Topological ergodicity of the family `(Φᵢ)`** — the "that is" clause of `def:egf`
(`main.tex:219–221`): for all `x, y` and every neighbourhood `U` of `y` there is a word
`i₁ ⋯ i_t` with `xΦ_{i₁}Φ_{i₂}⋯Φ_{i_t} ∈ U` (right action: `Φ_{i₁}` is applied first). -/
def IsTopologicallyErgodic [TopologicalSpace S] {p : ℕ} (Φ : Fin p → S → S) : Prop :=
  ∀ x y : S, ∀ U ∈ 𝓝 y, ∃ w : List (Fin p), w.foldl (fun z i => Φ i z) x ∈ U

/-- **An Ergodic Generative Flow** (`def:egf`, `main.tex:216–222`): a generative flow whose forward
policy is `π(s) = ∑ᵢ αⁱ(s) δ_{Φᵢ(s)}` for a family of homeomorphisms `Φᵢ` (diffeomorphisms in the
paper) and a policy `α`, the family being topologically ergodic. -/
structure IsEGF [TopologicalSpace S] (F : GenerativeFlow S) {p : ℕ} (Φ : Fin p → S ≃ₜ S)
    (α : Fin p → S → ℝ) : Prop where
  policy : IsEGFPolicy F.policy (fun i => Φ i) α
  ergodic : IsTopologicallyErgodic (fun i => (Φ i : S → S))

/-! ### Two readings of topological ergodicity -/

/-- The "that is" clause with non-empty words only (`t ≥ 1`). -/
def IsTopologicallyErgodicPos [TopologicalSpace S] {p : ℕ} (Φ : Fin p → S → S) : Prop :=
  ∀ x y : S, ∀ U ∈ 𝓝 y, ∃ w : List (Fin p), w ≠ [] ∧ w.foldl (fun z i => Φ i z) x ∈ U

omit [MeasurableSpace S] in
/-- With at least one map, allowing the empty word changes nothing. -/
theorem isTopologicallyErgodic_iff_pos [TopologicalSpace S] {p : ℕ} [NeZero p]
    (Φ : Fin p → S → S) : IsTopologicallyErgodic Φ ↔ IsTopologicallyErgodicPos Φ := by
  constructor
  · intro h x y U hU
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := h (Φ 0 x) y U hU
    exact ⟨0 :: w, List.cons_ne_nil _ _, by simpa using hw⟩
  · intro h x y U hU
    obtain ⟨w, -, hw⟩ := h x y U hU
    exact ⟨w, hw⟩

/-- Topological ergodicity of the **group** generated by the `Φᵢ`: words in the `Φᵢ` and their
inverses. -/
def IsTopologicallyErgodicGroup [TopologicalSpace S] {p : ℕ} (Φ : Fin p → S ≃ₜ S) : Prop :=
  ∀ x y : S, ∀ U ∈ 𝓝 y, ∃ w : List (Fin p × Bool),
    w.foldl (fun z ib => if ib.2 then Φ ib.1 z else (Φ ib.1).symm z) x ∈ U

omit [MeasurableSpace S] in
theorem IsTopologicallyErgodic.group [TopologicalSpace S] {p : ℕ} {Φ : Fin p → S ≃ₜ S}
    (h : IsTopologicallyErgodic fun i => (Φ i : S → S)) : IsTopologicallyErgodicGroup Φ := by
  intro x y U hU
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := h x y U hU
  refine ⟨w.map fun i => (i, true), ?_⟩
  simpa [List.foldl_map] using hw

/-- The translation `n ↦ n + 1` of `ℤ`. -/
def shiftZ : Fin 1 → ℤ ≃ₜ ℤ := fun _ => Homeomorph.addRight 1

theorem foldl_shiftZ_true (w : List (Fin 1)) (x : ℤ) :
    w.foldl (fun z i => (shiftZ i : ℤ → ℤ) z) x = x + w.length := by
  induction w generalizing x with
  | nil => simp
  | cons i w ih =>
      simp only [List.foldl_cons, List.length_cons, ih]
      simp [shiftZ]; ring

/-- **Finding** (`def:egf`, `main.tex:219–221`): the "that is" clause is strictly stronger than
topological ergodicity of the group it names. On `ℤ` (a `0`-manifold) the translation by `1`
generates a group whose orbits are all of `ℤ`, while its forward words never go down. -/
theorem shiftZ_group_not_forward :
    IsTopologicallyErgodicGroup shiftZ ∧ ¬ IsTopologicallyErgodic fun i => (shiftZ i : ℤ → ℤ) := by
  constructor
  · intro x y U hU
    have hy : y ∈ U := mem_of_mem_nhds hU
    have key : ∀ (n : ℕ) (b : Bool) (z : ℤ),
        (List.replicate n ((0 : Fin 1), b)).foldl
          (fun z ib => if ib.2 then shiftZ ib.1 z else (shiftZ ib.1).symm z) z
          = z + (if b then (n : ℤ) else -(n : ℤ)) := by
      intro n b
      induction n with
      | zero => intro z; cases b <;> simp
      | succ n ih =>
          intro z
          rw [List.replicate_succ, List.foldl_cons, ih]
          cases b <;> simp [shiftZ, Homeomorph.addRight_symm, Homeomorph.coe_addRight] <;> ring
    rcases le_total x y with hxy | hxy
    · refine ⟨List.replicate (y - x).toNat (0, true), ?_⟩
      rw [key]; simp only [if_true]
      rw [Int.toNat_of_nonneg (sub_nonneg.mpr hxy)]; simpa using hy
    · refine ⟨List.replicate (x - y).toNat (0, false), ?_⟩
      rw [key]
      simp only [Bool.false_eq_true, if_false]
      rw [Int.toNat_of_nonneg (sub_nonneg.mpr hxy)]; simpa using hy
  · intro h
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := h 0 (-1) {-1} (by simp)
    rw [foldl_shiftZ_true] at hw
    simp at hw

/-! ## Universal families (`def:universal_family`, `main.tex:249–252`) -/

/-- **A universal family of generative flows** (`def:universal_family`), with "distributions" read as
probability measures: for any two probability measures `μ, ν ≪ λ` with bounded density there is a
flow in the family that is flow matching for `F_init = ν`, `F_term = μ`. -/
def IsUniversalFamily (lam : Measure S) (𝓕 : Set (GenerativeFlow S)) : Prop :=
  ∀ μ ν : Measure S, IsProbabilityMeasure μ → IsProbabilityMeasure ν → μ ≪ lam → ν ≪ lam →
    (∃ C : ℝ≥0, ∀ᵐ s ∂lam, μ.rnDeriv lam s ≤ C) → (∃ C : ℝ≥0, ∀ᵐ s ∂lam, ν.rnDeriv lam s ≤ C) →
    ∃ F ∈ 𝓕, F.IsFlowMatching ν μ

/-- The other reading of `def:universal_family`: "distributions" as unnormalized (finite) measures.
It is never satisfied on a finite non-zero `λ` (`not_isUniversalFamilyUnnormalized`). -/
def IsUniversalFamilyUnnormalized (lam : Measure S) (𝓕 : Set (GenerativeFlow S)) : Prop :=
  ∀ μ ν : Measure S, IsFiniteMeasure μ → IsFiniteMeasure ν → μ ≪ lam → ν ≪ lam →
    (∃ C : ℝ≥0, ∀ᵐ s ∂lam, μ.rnDeriv lam s ≤ C) → (∃ C : ℝ≥0, ∀ᵐ s ∂lam, ν.rnDeriv lam s ≤ C) →
    ∃ F ∈ 𝓕, F.IsFlowMatching ν μ

/-! ## Summable `L²`-mixing (`def:summably_mixing`, `main.tex:262–269`) -/

/-- The iterated image measure `μ πⁿ` (`main.tex:158`, iterated). -/
noncomputable def pushIter (π : Kernel S S) (n : ℕ) (μ : Measure S) : Measure S :=
  (fun ρ : Measure S => ρ.bind π)^[n] μ

/-- **`φ πⁿ := d((φλ)πⁿ)/dλ`**, the `n`-th power of the Koopman operator `φ ↦ d((φλ)π)/dλ` of
`main.tex:273`, on a signed density `φ`, through `φ⁺` and `φ⁻` (template:
`GFNBounds.Core.densityAction`, `lean/GFNBounds/Core/Kernel.lean`, here iterated on measures). -/
noncomputable def transfer (π : Kernel S S) (lam : Measure S) (n : ℕ) (φ : S → ℝ) : S → ℝ :=
  fun s => ((pushIter π n (lam.withDensity fun x => ENNReal.ofReal (φ x))).rnDeriv lam s).toReal
    - ((pushIter π n (lam.withDensity fun x => ENNReal.ofReal (-φ x))).rnDeriv lam s).toReal

/-- **The set `H`** of `def:summably_mixing`: `φ ∈ L²(λ)`, `‖φ‖₂ = 1`, `∫ φ dλ = 0`. -/
def unitMeanZero (lam : Measure S) : Set (S → ℝ) :=
  {φ | MemLp φ 2 lam ∧ eLpNorm φ 2 lam = 1 ∧ ∫ s, φ s ∂lam = 0}

/-- **The `L²`-mixing coefficient** `γₙ := sup_{φ ∈ H} ∫ (φπⁿ)² dλ̂`, in `ℝ≥0∞`. -/
noncomputable def mixingCoeff (π : Kernel S S) (lam lamHat : Measure S) (n : ℕ) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ⨆ φ ∈ unitMeanZero lam, ∫⁻ s, ENNReal.ofReal (transfer π lam n φ s ^ 2) ∂lamHat

/-- **Summably `L²`-mixing** (`def:summably_mixing`): `π` admits an invariant measure `λ̂`
equivalent to `λ` whose mixing coefficients are summable. -/
def IsSummablyL2Mixing (π : Kernel S S) (lam : Measure S) : Prop :=
  ∃ lamHat : Measure S, lamHat.bind π = lamHat ∧ lamHat ≪ lam ∧ lam ≪ lamHat ∧
    ∑' n, mixingCoeff π lam lamHat n ≠ ∞

/-! ## The unnormalized reading of `def:universal_family` is empty -/

/-- **Finding.** Read with unnormalized distributions, `def:universal_family` is never satisfied
on a finite non-zero `λ`: flow matching from `ν = λ` to `μ = 2λ` would force `λ(𝒮) = 2λ(𝒮)`. -/
theorem not_isUniversalFamilyUnnormalized (lam : Measure S) [IsFiniteMeasure lam] (hlam : lam ≠ 0)
    (𝓕 : Set (GenerativeFlow S)) : ¬ IsUniversalFamilyUnnormalized lam 𝓕 := by
  intro h
  have h1 : ∃ C : ℝ≥0, ∀ᵐ s ∂lam, lam.rnDeriv lam s ≤ C :=
    ⟨1, (Measure.rnDeriv_self lam).mono fun s hs => by simp [hs]⟩
  have h2 : ∃ C : ℝ≥0, ∀ᵐ s ∂lam, ((2 : ℝ≥0) • lam).rnDeriv lam s ≤ C := by
    refine ⟨2, ?_⟩
    filter_upwards [Measure.rnDeriv_smul_left lam lam (2 : ℝ≥0),
      Measure.rnDeriv_self lam] with s hs hs'
    simp [hs, hs']
  obtain ⟨F, -, heq⟩ := h ((2 : ℝ≥0) • lam) lam inferInstance inferInstance
    (Measure.AbsolutelyContinuous.rfl.smul_left 2) Measure.AbsolutelyContinuous.rfl h2 h1
  have := congrArg (fun m : Measure S => m Set.univ) heq
  simp only [inflow, Measure.add_apply, Measure.smul_apply, bind_univ] at this
  have hF' : F.outflow Set.univ ≠ ∞ := measure_ne_top _ _
  have hl : lam Set.univ = (2 : ℝ≥0) • lam Set.univ := (ENNReal.add_left_inj hF').1 this
  have hl0 : lam Set.univ ≠ 0 := by simpa [Measure.measure_univ_eq_zero] using hlam
  have hlt : lam Set.univ ≠ ∞ := measure_ne_top _ _
  have hr := congrArg ENNReal.toReal hl
  rw [ENNReal.smul_def, smul_eq_mul, ENNReal.toReal_mul] at hr
  have hpos : 0 < (lam Set.univ).toReal := ENNReal.toReal_pos hl0 hlt
  norm_num at hr
  linarith

end EGF
